ad and cadmium in tree-rings of eastern red-cedar</article-title><source>J Environ Qual</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>146</fpage><lpage>150</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp0115-000715"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Hagemeyer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group> 1993. Monitoring trace metal pollution with tree rings: a critical reassessment. In: Plants as Biomonitors: Indicators for Heavy Metals in the Terrestrial Environment (Markert B, ed). New York:VCN Weinheim, 541&#x02013;563.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp0115-000715"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Hagemeyer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinand</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Radial distributions of Pb in stems of young Norway spruce trees grown in Pb-contaminated soil</article-title><source>Tree Phys</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>591</fpage><lpage>594</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="b13-ehp0115-000715"><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><person-group><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name><name><surname>Humphreys</surname><given-names>DSC</given-names></name></person-group> 1983. Tungsten: A Review. No. 2. London:Institution of Mining and Metallurgy, Occasional Papers of the Institution of Mining and Metallurgy. IARC. 2003. Cobalt in Hard-metals and Cobalt Sulfate, Gallium Arsenide, Indium Phosphide and Vanadium Pentoxide.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-ehp0115-000715"><mixed-citation publication-type="other">IARC Monogr Eval Carcinog Risk Hum 86. Available: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://monographs.iarc.fr/ENG/Meetings/vol86.php">http://monographs.iarc.fr/ENG/Meetings/vol86.php</ext-link> [accessed 13 February 2007].</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-ehp0115-000715"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-gro